  "passage": "In social studies class, students learned that countries sometimes make agreements to protect parts of the ocean beyond national borders.\nThe teacher explained that no single country owns all oceans, but many countries use them. Fishing, shipping, mining, and pollution can affect shared waters.\nStudents played a negotiation game. Each group represented a country with different needs. They quickly found that protecting shared resources was difficult.\nIf one group took too much, others suffered. If no one trusted each other, the agreement failed.\nThe game made international cooperation feel real. A shared ocean needs shared rules, or everyone loses.",
